.TH CHECKPOINT 1 "September 2026" "Universal Linux" "Snapshot Manager"
.SH NAME
checkpoint \- Universal snapshot manager using Timeshift and Snapper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B checkpoint
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fISUBCOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B checkpoint
is a system state capture tool that provides advanced retention logic for Timeshift and Snapper snapshots. It allows for "undeletable" snapshots and ensures that system state archives are managed efficiently across different Linux distributions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B create
Explicitly create a new system snapshot (default action when invoked without arguments).
.TP
.BR \-nc ", " \-\-no\-cleanup
Create snapshot without running cleanup.
.TP
.BR \-cl ", " \-\-cleanup\-only
Run snapshot cleanup logic only (keeping last \fIN\fR normal snapshots).
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List existing snapshots in a clean, formatted table.
.TP
.BR \-ch ", " \-\-check
Check snapshot backend readiness and exit.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-delete " [\fIPATTERN\fR]"
Interactive deletion menu via \fBfzf\fR, or targeted deletion matching pattern.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-comment " \fIMSG\fR"
Add a custom comment to the snapshot.
.TP
.BR \-ks ", " \-\-keep\-snapshot
Make the new snapshot undeletable by appending \fB[KEEP]\fR to the comment.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force\-delete
Override protection and delete \fB[KEEP]\fR snapshots during cleanup or deletion.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep " \fIN\fR"
Limit cleanup to keep the last \fIN\fR normal snapshots. Protected snapshots are not counted towards this limit.
.TP
.BR \-\-backend " \fINAME\fR"
Override snapshot backend driver for this run (e.g. \fBsnapper\fR, \fBtimeshift\-btrfs\fR, \fBtimeshift\-rsync\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-porcelain
Output strict machine-readable \fBKEY="VALUE"\fR metadata to stdout for IPC with Advance or automated scripts.
.TP
.BR \-\-type " \fItype\fR"
Snapshot type for paired snapshots: \fBsingle\fR, \fBpre\fR, or \fBpost\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-pre\-id " \fIID\fR"
Specify pre-snapshot ID when creating a \fBpost\fR snapshot with paired backends (e.g. Snapper).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-rsync
Force RSYNC snapshot mode.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-btrfs
Force BTRFS snapshot mode.
.TP
.BR \-sd ", " \-\-snapshot\-device " \fIDEV\fR"
Override backup target storage device or partition.
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-self\-update ", " \-\-selfupdate
Update Checkpoint from the local git repository and reinstall.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-changelog " [" \fIVERSION\fR "]"
Display formatted release notes from the changelog. If executed interactively in a terminal without arguments and \fBfzf\fR is available, launches an interactive version browser.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose ", " \-\-debug
Enable detailed execution logs for troubleshooting.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command usage and options summary.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B check
Verify whether a snapshot backend is installed, active, and operational. Exits 0 if ready, 1 otherwise. Supports \fB\-\-porcelain\fR for automated IPC.
.TP
.B changelog \fR[\fIVERSION\fR]
Browse interactive release history or print formatted release notes for a specific version (or \fB\-\-latest\fR).
.TP
.B config
Launch interactive configuration wizard via \fBfzf\fR to configure snapshot limits, retention rules, and default backend settings.
.TP
.BR self\-update ", " selfupdate
Pull latest changes from the local source git repository and reinstall.
.SH RETENTION LOGIC
.B checkpoint
uses a specialized counting algorithm for cleanup:
.IP 1. 4
It iterates through snapshots from newest to oldest.
.IP 2. 4
If a snapshot comment contains \fB[KEEP]\fR, it is skipped and remains on the disk indefinitely.
.IP 3. 4
The counter only increments for "normal" snapshots.
.IP 4. 4
Once the counter exceeds the limit (Default: 6), older normal snapshots are deleted.
.SH CONFIGURATION FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/checkpoint/config
Main configuration file in \fBKEY=VALUE\fR format. Managed via \fBcheckpoint config\fR. Key settings include:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSNAPSHOT_BACKEND\fR: Active snapshot backend recipe (\fBauto\fR, \fBsnapper\fR, \fBtimeshift\-btrfs\fR, \fBtimeshift\-rsync\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDEFAULT_KEEP_LIMIT\fR: Number of unprotected normal snapshots to retain during cleanup (Default: \fB6\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBALWAYS_KEEP\fR: Automatically mark every new snapshot as protected [KEEP] (\fBtrue\fR or \fBfalse\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBALWAYS_CREATE\fR: Automatically create snapshot when invoked without flags (\fBtrue\fR or \fBfalse\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBALWAYS_CLEANUP\fR: Automatically prune old snapshots exceeding limit when invoked without flags (\fBtrue\fR or \fBfalse\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAUTO_RETRIES\fR: Number of automatic retries before prompting the user (Default: \fB1\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBINFINITE_RETRIES\fR: Retry failed operations endlessly without prompting (\fBtrue\fR or \fBfalse\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSNAPSHOT_DEVICE\fR: Override default backup device partition or UUID.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSELF_UPDATE_CHECK\fR: Automatic self-update detector mode (\fBprompt\fR, \fBnotify\fR, \fBauto\fR, or \fBoff\fR; Default: \fBprompt\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBUSE_COLOR\fR / \fBUSE_EMOJI\fR: UI display preferences (\fBtrue\fR or \fBfalse\fR).
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR advance (1),
.BR snapper (8),
.BR timeshift (1)
